# Skin and UV Layout

## Reference
See `docs/minecraft-skin-layout-specification.md` for full pixel-level spec.

## Layer Bounds (64×64)
| Layer | Region (X, Y, W, H) |
|-------|---------------------|
| Head | 0–32, 0–16 |
| Hat | 32–64, 0–16 |
| Body | 16–32, 16–32 |
| Jacket | 16–32, 32–48 |
| Arms | 40–56 (right), 32–48 (left) |
| Sleeves | 40–56 (right), 48–64 (left) |
| Legs | 0–16 (right), 16–32 (left) |
| Pants | 0–16, 32–48 (right), 0–16, 48–64 (left) |

## Pixel Art Display
- `image-rendering: pixelated`
- `ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false`

## Preprocessing
- `skinPreprocess.ts` — transparency handling in primary regions
- `SKIN_PREPROCESS_CONFIG`: enabled, replacementColor, alphaThreshold

## Overlay Meshes
- `renderOrder = 1` for hat, jacket, sleeves, pants
- Optional `OVERLAY_SCALE.factor` (e.g. 1.03) for jacket/sleeves/pants
